  "articleBody": "It’s a question we hear a lot: \"Can I just tile right over my old wall finish?\" While it might seem like a shortcut, it really depends on what's currently on your wall. Generally, if you have old, peeling paint, wallpaper, or an uneven surface, you're going to need to do some prep work. Installing tile over an unstable or dirty surface is a recipe for disaster, as the tiles won't adhere properly and could eventually fall off. You'll need a flat, clean, and sound surface for the best results. Often, this means removing old adhesive, repairing damaged areas, and making sure the wall is perfectly plumb and square. For wet areas, like showers, specific moisture-resistant backer materials are absolutely crucial. Don't take chances here! If you're unsure about your wall's condition or what kind of prep it needs, getting a professional assessment is smart. HH Remodeling LLC can help evaluate your walls and recommend the best approach to ensure your new wall tile lasts.",
